-- title:
--   Mutual integrality of j and j(qᵈ) at level M
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $M, q, d$ with $M \neq 0$, $d \neq 0$ and $q$ prime, and assume $d \mid M$. Let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M` be the intermediate field of $\mathbf{Q}((q))$ (Laurent series over $\mathbf{Q}$) generated over $\mathbf{Q}$ by the elements `qExpand ℚ e jq` for the nonzero divisors $e$ of $M$, where `jq` is $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNumQ` and `qExpand ℚ e` is the ring endomorphism of Laurent series multiplying all exponents by $e$ (substitution $q \mapsto q^{e}$). Put $j_d \in F$ for the element `qExpand ℚ d jq`, and let `jFull M` $\in F$ be `jq` itself. Write $R =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt q`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the base ring for which `chartAlg M q S` is the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $S$. The assertion is threefold: $j_d \neq 0$; $j_d$ lies in `chartAlgFin M q`, i.e. is integral over $R[\,$`jFull M`$\,]$; and `jFull M` is integral over $R[\,j_d\,]$.
--
--   Classically this is the statement that $j$ and $j(q^{d})$ satisfy the modular equation $\Phi_d(X,Y) = 0$, monic of degree $\psi(d)$ in each variable, so that each is integral over the ring generated by the other. It is what allows the two-chart Igusa-type model of the modular function field to be built from the generator $j(q^{d})$ as well as from $j$, and it feeds the degeneracy and local-model statements at Deligne–Rapoport level that cite it.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_IgusaScheme_qExpand_jq_mem_chartAlgFin_and_jFull_mem_chartAlg.lean

